<title>USA: BOXING-BOUDOUANI RETAINS TITLE.</title>
<headline>BOXING-BOUDOUANI RETAINS TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laurent Boudouani of France retained his World Boxing Association junior middleweight crown with a unanimous decision over American Carl Daniels on Saturday.</p>
<p>Judge Marcial Vargas scored it 118-108 for the Boudouani, while Melchior Taylor had it 115-111 and Duane Ford 117-109.</p>
<p>Boudouani is 35-2, and Daniels fell to 38-3.</p>
</text>
